  "modules": [
    {
      "module": 1,
      "questions": [
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q1",
          "number": 1,
          "domain": "Craft and Structure",
          "skill": "Words in Context",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "The Caves of Gargas paintings--stencils of human hands found in what is now France and dating from around 27000 years ago--are thought of as art today, but the question of whether the people of the time understood the paintings as something akin to art in our modern sense or in some other way entirely is _____; we will never be able to answer it.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical and precise word or phrase?",
          "options": {
            "A": "irresolvable",
            "B": "self-contradictory",
            "C": "imperative",
            "D": "unavoidable"
          },
          "answer": "A",
          "explanation": "If we will 'never be able to answer it', the question is irresolvable.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q2",
          "number": 2,
          "domain": "Information and Ideas",
          "skill": "Inferences",
          "difficulty": "hard",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "In a 2012 study in the United States, Michael E. Berndt and Travis K. Bavin found a positive association between levels of dissolved organic carbon and mercury in bodies of fresh water. Many other studies have yielded similar results... But much of that research has been conducted at broadly similar sites in North America, and when Seam Noh and colleagues examined bodies of fresh water in South Korea, they found a negative association... If similar findings emerge from other locations outside North America, that could suggest that _____",
          "question": "Which choice most logically completes the text?",
          "options": {
            "A": "the mercury levels reported in Noh...",
            "B": "Berndt and Bavin may have inadvertently measured...",
            "C": "the relationship between dissolved organic carbon and mercury reported by Berndt and Bavin reflects conditions that are characteristic of certain kinds of ecosystems rather than universal conditions.",
            "D": "most of the studies conducted in North America have measured..."
          },
          "answer": "C",
          "explanation": "The text contrasts North American findings (positive association) with non-North American findings (negative association). Thus, the North American results likely reflect local ecosystem conditions rather than universal laws.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q3",
          "number": 3,
          "domain": "Standard English Conventions",
          "skill": "Boundaries",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "In the thought-provoking 2010 exhibition Relative Pelican at the Stux Gallery in New York, Sokari Douglas Camp presented sculptures that had been _____ welded from recycled metal materials, such as oil drums. In doing so, the London-based Nigerian sculptor challenged viewers to imagine new uses and futures for the material wastes of the past.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
          "options": {
            "A": "cut, bent, and,",
            "B": "cut, bent, and",
            "C": "cut, bent; and",
            "D": "cut bent, and"
          },
          "answer": "B",
          "explanation": "Standard list format: 'cut, bent, and' directly modifies 'welded' without needing an extraneous comma before 'welded'.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q4",
          "number": 4,
          "domain": "Standard English Conventions",
          "skill": "Form, Structure, and Sense",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "In Puerto Rico, it's not unusual for a city or town to be known _____ a nickname that corresponds to one of its notable features, like landscape, climate, famous residents, or chief exports. For example, the Puerto Rican municipality of Hatillo has also been called \"the Land of Green Fields,\" a nickname that alludes to what the area is well known for: the lush greenery that surrounds it.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
          "options": {
            "A": "by",
            "B": "by-",
            "C": "by,",
            "D": "by:"
          },
          "answer": "A",
          "explanation": "The preposition 'by' seamlessly links the verb 'known' to its object 'a nickname' without requiring punctuation.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q5",
          "number": 5,
          "domain": "Standard English Conventions",
          "skill": "Form, Structure, and Sense",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "In 2021, Sarah McAnulty _____ as a biologist at the University of Connecticut, studying squids.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
          "options": {
            "A": "working",
            "B": "was working",
            "C": "to work",
            "D": "to have worked"
          },
          "answer": "B",
          "explanation": "The sentence requires a main verb. 'was working' serves to create a complete independent clause.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q6",
          "number": 6,
          "domain": "Standard English Conventions",
          "skill": "Form, Structure, and Sense",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "The word \"robot\" _____ first used in the 1920 play R.U.R. by Czech author Karel Capek.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
          "options": {
            "A": "were",
            "B": "were being",
            "C": "was",
            "D": "have been"
          },
          "answer": "C",
          "explanation": "The subject 'word' is singular, so it requires the singular past tense verb 'was'.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q7",
          "number": 7,
          "domain": "Standard English Conventions",
          "skill": "Form, Structure, and Sense",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "In the spring of 1964, it was hard to go anywhere without hearing the song \"Cotton Candy\" by the Sylvers. As of April 11, the song had spent thirteen straight weeks on the Billboard Hot 100 chart and _____ No.1 on the list.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
          "options": {
            "A": "have been ranking",
            "B": "was ranked",
            "C": "were ranked",
            "D": "are ranking"
          },
          "answer": "B",
          "explanation": "The singular subject 'song' in past tense requires 'was ranked' to maintain parallel tense and agreement with 'had spent'.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q8",
          "number": 8,
          "domain": "Standard English Conventions",
          "skill": "Form, Structure, and Sense",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "In 2000, the United States Congress designated a portion of Pennsylvania as the Lackawanna Valley National Heritage Area, _____ the region's unique natural, cultural, and historical attributes.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text so that it conforms to the conventions of Standard English?",
          "options": {
            "A": "they cite",
            "B": "cited",
            "C": "citing",
            "D": "has cited"
          },
          "answer": "C",
          "explanation": "A participle phrase 'citing...' modifies the preceding clause. 'Citing' correctly relates the action to Congress designating the area.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q9",
          "number": 9,
          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "skill": "Transitions",
          "difficulty": "easy",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "In 1940, scientists first isolated a sample of the steroid hormone androstenone, which they knew existed in animals--and, they assumed, only in animals. _____ scientists know that androstenone can also be found in chokecherry plants (Prunus virginiana), but this discovery didn't occur until decades later.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",
          "options": {
            "A": "Today,",
            "B": "For instance,",
            "C": "In other words,",
            "D": "Thus,"
          },
          "answer": "A",
          "explanation": "The text contrasts what scientists thought in 1940 with what they know 'Today' or now.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q10",
          "number": 10,
          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "skill": "Transitions",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "According to traditional classifications, each of William Shakespeare's plays belongs to one of three distinct genres: comedy, history, or tragedy. The play Much Ado About Nothing (1598-99), _____ is classified as a comedy, whereas Richard II (1595) is classified as a history.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",
          "options": {
            "A": "in addition,",
            "B": "similarly,",
            "C": "for instance,",
            "D": "however,"
          },
          "answer": "C",
          "explanation": "'for instance' seamlessly introduces the examples of comedy and history plays that match the previous sentence's classification scheme.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q11",
          "number": 11,
          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "skill": "Transitions",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "If you were to view the Ol Kokwe volcano in Kenya or the Asavyo volcano in Ethiopia from above, you might notice that their low profiles and gently sloping sides make each of them look a bit like a shield lying flat on the ground. _____ volcanologists classify volcanoes of this type as shield volcanoes.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",
          "options": {
            "A": "Still,",
            "B": "Besides,",
            "C": "Second,",
            "D": "Fittingly,"
          },
          "answer": "D",
          "explanation": "Because they look like shields, it is fitting (appropriate) that they are classified as shield volcanoes.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q12",
          "number": 12,
          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "skill": "Transitions",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "Though its onboard laboratory allowed it to analyze rock samples on site, the 2011 Mars Curiosity rover was unable to preserve samples for future analysis. _____ when creating the 2020 Mars Perseverance rover, robotics mechanical engineer Arash Kalantari and other members of NASA's Jet Propulsion Laboratory sought to implement a mechanism that could do exactly that.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",
          "options": {
            "A": "Previously,",
            "B": "Specifically,",
            "C": "Likewise,",
            "D": "Thus,"
          },
          "answer": "D",
          "explanation": "Because Curiosity lacked the ability, 'Thus' introduces the consequence: the team aimed to implement it in the next rover.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q13",
          "number": 13,
          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "skill": "Transitions",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "Though the musical groups Los Palominos and Banda Los Recoditos are often categorized under the catchall \"regional Mexican music\" label, they each adhere to distinct musical traditions. The former works within the tejano tradition, which originated in mid-twentieth-century Texas and northern Mexico. The latter,_____ follows the banda tradition, with roots in min-nineteenth-century southern and central Mexico.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",
          "options": {
            "A": "therefore,",
            "B": "by contrast,",
            "C": "however,",
            "D": "in other words,"
          },
          "answer": "B",
          "explanation": "The text sets up a contrast between the first group's style (tejano) and the second group's style (banda), so 'by contrast' fits perfectly.",
          "points": 1
        },
        {
          "id": "2023-june-m1-q14",
          "number": 14,
          "domain": "Expression of Ideas",
          "skill": "Transitions",
          "difficulty": "medium",
          "type": "multiple_choice",
          "passage": "Water from the aquifers of Alaska's Susitna Glacier travels the 160 km length of the Skwentna River before flowing into the Yentna River and then reaching the mouth of the river system's main stem, the Susitna River. _____ at the Susitna's mouth, hundreds of kilometers from the source, the water empties into the Gulf of Alaska.",
          "question": "Which choice completes the text with the most logical transition?",
          "options": {
            "A": "There,",
            "B": "For instance,",
            "C": "Regardless,",
            "D": "Finally,"
          },
          "answer": "D",
          "explanation": "'Finally,' correctly indicates the last step in the chronological flow of the water journey described.",
          "points": 1
        },
